  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="DA">Social Cohesion Strengthening through Improved Inter faith groups relation in South Kordofan State in Sudan- phase 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="DA">This intervention&#x2019;s efforts will help to ensure that social cohesion is strengthened through the promotion of positive interfaith relations in South Kordofan where the minority faith groups will be able to fully enjoy their freedom of religion and belief as part of their human rights. This will be achieved through emphasis on recognition and respect for human rights as well as the inclusion of gender and minority faith groups in all aspects of social interactions in Sudan. 
From a human rights perspective, the target groups will be engaged through discussions and reflections particularly on the provisions of article 18 of the International Covenant on Civil and Political Rights (ICCPR), on which freedom of religion and belief is anchored. The &#x201C;heart of FoRB&#x201D; will be prioritized and broken down into practical application details as under; 
1)	The freedom to have, choose, change or leave a religion or belief and
2)	The freedom to practice or manifest a religion or belief.
Depending on the comprehension level of the target audience, other rights under FoRB will be covered as under;
3)	The right to protection from coercion and
4)	from discrimination in matters of religion or belief,
5)	The rights for parents and for children concerning religion and belief,
6)	The right to conscientious objection.</narrative>
  </description>
